326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 274 0 R
/E (The increasing volume of medical imaging examinations presents significant challenges to diagnostic radiology, including increased radiologist workload, diagnostic errors, and inter-observer variability. This requires the development of robust, automated systems to support clinical decision-making. This research addresses this challenge by proposing and implementing DeepDiagnose, an intelligent multi-agent Artificial Intelligence platform for the detection of diverse pathologies across multiple imaging modalities. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 274 0 R
/E (The system employs an innovative "chain-of-thought" workflow, routing images through specialized ConvolutionalNeural Network \(CNN\) agents for the initial classification of COVID-19, Pneumonia, andOsteoarthritis from CT and X-ray images. For diagnostically ambiguous cases where theprimary model's confidence is low, the system automatically flags the finding as "Uncertain," ensuring it is escalated for mandatory review by a human expert. The )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 274 0 R
/E (entire platform is engineeredon a secure, asynchronous three-tier architecture using FastAPI, )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 274 0 R
/E (with a complete frameworkfor AI explainability and continuous improvement. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 274 0 R
/E (The specialist CNN models,developed using a transfer learning approach with the )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 274 0 R
/E (EfficientNetB0 architecture,were rigorously evaluated. The models achieved high diagnostic accuracy, with a particularfocus on clinical safety, consistently reaching a target Recall of over 90% for critical conditionslike Pneumonia and COVID-19, thereby minimizing false negatives. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
