<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 282 0 R
/E (This chapter reviews the existing literature relevant to the application of Artificial Intelligence \(AI\) in medical imaging for disease detection. It begins by establishing the context of deep learning in modern healthcare, then narrows its focus to the specific Convolutional Neural NEtwork \(CNN\) architectures that are foundation to this project. Subsequently, it examines the current state of research for the three specific medical conditions under investigation: Pneumonia, COVID-19, and Osteoarthritis. Finally, this review identifies a critical gap in the existing research concerning unified, multi-disease diagnostic systems, thereby establishing the academic justification for this project. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
