/P 282 0 R
/E (The work by Krizhevsky et al. \(2012\) with the AlexxNet model demonstrated that CNNs could automatically learn hierarchical feature representations directly pixel data, capability that is exceptionally well suited for analysing complex medical scans. A key enabler for the application of these powerful models in medicine, where datasets can be limited, is the technique of transfer learning. As shown by Shin et al. \(2016\), pre-training a model on a large natural image dataset and then fine-tuning it on medical images allows for the development of a high performing )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [8]
>>
