697 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 306 0 R
/E (A core feature of the system's design is the confidence-based mechanism to handle diagnostic uncertainty. The COVID-19 prediction logic, for example, was implemented with specific confidence thresholds \(90% for a positive finding, 80% for normal\). During testing, this system successfully identified and flagged cases that fell between these thresholds as "Uncertain - Consult Specialist," fulfilling its role as a critical safety feature to escalate ambiguous cases for human expert review. )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
698 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 306 0 R
/T (4.2 System Performance and Operational Metrics )
/E (4.2 System Performance and Operational Metrics )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
699 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 306 0 R
/E (Beyond the diagnostic accuracy of the individual specialist models, the overall operational performance of the system was also evaluated. The initial routing models for scan type and anatomy classification performed reliably during development and testing, successfully directing all test images to the appropriate specialist pipelines. The asynchronous architecture of the FastAPI backend, which processes each prediction request in a non-blocking )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
700 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 306 0 R
/E (ThreadPoolExecutor, was designed for efficiency and to ensure the system remains responsive under load. )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [4]
>>
