735 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 312 0 R
/E (The results presented in the previous chapter demonstrate that our intelligent, multi-agent AI system achieved high performance across all diagnostic tasks. The specialist CNN models, built using a transfer learning approach, exhibited strong recall, consistently meeting our target of over 90% for critical conditions like COVID-19. This outcome validates our methodology of prioritizing clinical safety by minimizing false negatives. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
736 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 312 0 R
/E (The high accuracy of the initial routing and triage models was crucial to the success of the )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
737 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 312 0 R
/E (overall pipeline, confirming the viability of a multi-step diagnostic workflow. This approach, which routes images to specialized models, proved to be both efficient and effective. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
738 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 312 0 R
/E (Perhaps the most significant finding, from a clinical safety perspective, was the successful implementation of the confidence-based uncertainty handling mechanism. The system's ability to identify and flag a meaningful percentage of diagnostically ambiguous cases as "Uncertain - Consult Specialist" validates our approach. It demonstrates that the system does not overstate its own capabilities and successfully functions as a safe screening tool that knows when to escalate )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
739 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 312 0 R
/E (a case for mandatory review by a human expert. This supports our central hypothesis that a multi-agent architecture with built-in confidence checks can provide a robust and trustworthy diagnostic aid. )
/Pg 49 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
