/E (1. A Novel Multi-Agent Diagnostic Architecture: We designed and validated an )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
744 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (intelligent multi-agent diagnostic workflow that represents a departure from traditional, single-model approaches. Our system uses a "chain-of-thought" pipeline with specialized CNN agents for triage \(scan type and anatomy\) and diagnosis. A key innovation is the integrated, confidence-based mechanism that automatically flags uncertain cases for mandatory review by a human expert. This architecture provides a new, scalable template for developing comprehensive and clinically safe AI systems that can handle diverse conditions. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
745 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (2. A Framework for Responsible AI Communication: We developed a sophisticated )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
746 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (explainability \(XAI\) subsystem that goes beyond simple predictions. By generating audience-aware explanations for both patients and clinicians, our work provides a practical blueprint for responsible and effective human-AI communication in a sensitive medical context. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
747 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
